  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 802.02 Agronomic rate",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 802.02 “Agronomic rate” means the sludge application rate that is designed to:\n\n(a) Provide the amount of nitrogen, phosphorus, or other nutrient(s) needed by the crop or vegetation; and\n\n(b) Minimize the amount of nitrogen that passes below the root zone of the crop or the vegetation to groundwater or the amount of phosphorus that runs off to surface water.\n\nSource. #10998, eff 1-1-16; ss by #14571, eff 5-15-26, EXPIRES: 5-15-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq800.html"
